  "published": "2026-09-15T09:25:19.933Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.4: README fixes - the \"order create/get/capture\" CLI flow is now called out outside the ASP.NET Core section, added an \"Updating\" guide, and the Quickstart order-creation example now sets application_context.return_url/cancel_url so PayPal's approval page actually redirects the buyer back instead of leaving them on PayPal's own page with no confirmation. No library code changes. 1.2.3: Realigned the package version with the repo's git tag numbering (previously the git tags had drifted ahead of the published NuGet version) - no code changes. 1.0.3: Expanded the README's Sandbox payment walkthrough (the create/approve/capture flow, and using a Sandbox buyer account to approve an order). No code changes. 1.0.2: Fixed a real bug found testing against live Sandbox - bodyless POST/PUT/PATCH calls (Orders.CaptureAsync, Orders.AuthorizeAsync, Payments.RefundCaptureAsync, Payments.CaptureAuthorizationAsync, Webhooks.ResendEventNotificationAsync with no overrides) were rejected by PayPal with 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE because no Content-Type header was sent; the gateway now attaches an empty JSON body with Content-Type: application/json whenever the caller doesn't supply one for a write method. 1.0.1: Added net9.0 as an explicit target framework alongside netstandard2.0/net8.0/net10.0 for broader compatibility. Added a PartnerId fallback on Partner Referral calls. 1.0.0: Initial release - Partner Referrals, Orders/Checkout, Payments, Webhooks with signature verification, Vault, Apple Pay, Shipment Tracking, and Managed Accounts (limited release), plus automatic OAuth2 token caching.",
